          "value": "60797",
          "source": "script",
          "manual": false
        },
        {
          "field": "name_es",
          "value": "Chrono Cross",
          "source": "igdb",
          "manual": false
        },
        {
          "field": "original_name",
          "value": "Chrono Cross",
          "source": "igdb",
          "manual": false
        },
        {
          "field": "summary",
          "value": "CHRONO CROSS, the sequel to the SNES favorite CHRONO TRIGGER, is one of the most ambitious role-playing games ever made. There are over 40 playable characters, each with their back-story, special moves, abilities, and weapons. The story spans two discs and follows the story of Serge, a young man who is able to cross dimensions. Suddenly he is pulled between worlds, trying to figure out his own past at the same time. The graphics are bright and beautiful, utilizing the PlayStation's capabilities to the fullest. The polygonal character models are huge and detailed, and the pre-rendered backgrounds are immaculately detailed. The music is composed and arranged by Yasunori Mitsuda, and features very realistic-sounding synthesizers. The battle system revolves around Elements, which are used to grant magical powers, as well as to summon huge monsters. For anyone that wanted to see the story of CHRONO TRIGGER continue, this is your chance.",
          "source": "igdb",
          "manual": false
        },
        {
          "field": "summary_es",
          "value": "CHRONO CROSS, la secuela del favorito de SNES CHRONO TRIGGER, es uno de los juegos de rol más ambiciosos jamás creados. Tiene más de 40 personajes jugables, cada uno con su propia historia de fondo, movimientos especiales, habilidades y armas. La historia abarca dos discos y sigue a Serge, un joven capaz de cruzar dimensiones. De pronto se ve arrastrado entre mundos, mientras intenta descubrir al mismo tiempo su propio pasado. Los gráficos son luminosos y bellos, y aprovechan al máximo las capacidades de PlayStation. Los modelos poligonales de los personajes son grandes y detallados, y los fondos prerrenderizados tienen un detalle impecable. La música está compuesta y arreglada por Yasunori Mitsuda, y presenta sintetizadores de sonido muy realista. El sistema de combate gira en torno a los Elementos, que se usan para otorgar poderes mágicos y para invocar monstruos enormes. Para quien quisiera ver cómo continúa la historia de CHRONO TRIGGER, esta es su oportunidad.",
          "source": "claude",
          "manual": false
        },
        {
          "field": "year",
          "value": "1999",
          "source": "igdb",
          "manual": false
        }
      ],
